      "id": "xa50acq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Composition of the Atmosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Earth's atmosphere is structurally divided into five major layers: Troposphere, Stratosphere, Mesosphere, Thermosphere, and Exosphere.",
        "The Troposphere is the atmospheric layer closest to Earth where all critical weather phenomena occur.",
        "The Stratosphere houses the ozone layer, which shields the Earth by absorbing harmful ultraviolet solar radiation.",
        "Meteors burn up in the Mesosphere upon atmospheric entry due to high friction.",
        "The Thermosphere contains the ionosphere, crucial for long-distance radio communication."
      ],
      "id": "apvtpix"
    },
